WEBVTT

00:05.640 --> 00:08.350
What's gotten into you, Takada?

00:09.110 --> 00:13.290
I can't get Nishimura-san 
off my mind lately.

00:14.460 --> 00:16.490
That's always the case with you!

00:16.490 --> 00:18.670
Maybe so, but...

00:19.090 --> 00:20.370
<i>Could it be love?</i>

00:20.370 --> 00:22.150
<i>Isn't that the face of someone in love?</i>

00:24.420 --> 00:27.330
You're always hanging out 
with the Grim Reaper!

00:27.330 --> 00:29.580
Yep, because it's so much fun!

00:29.580 --> 00:34.220
But recently, I kinda feel my chest 
tighten up for some reason!

00:34.220 --> 00:36.480
Must be her curse!

00:36.480 --> 00:37.580
<i>That's love!</i>

00:37.580 --> 00:39.550
<i>

00:42.430 --> 00:43.990
Serves you right!</i>

00:43.990 --> 00:47.420
You're finally feeling
the effects of her curse!

00:47.420 --> 00:49.510
What? Finally?!

00:49.510 --> 00:50.980
Hooray!

00:50.980 --> 00:53.340
Now I can be pals with the Grim Reaper!

00:53.340 --> 00:55.210
Yay! Yay!

00:53.770 --> 00:55.750
How is <i>that</i> your conclusion?!

00:56.150 --> 00:59.210
<i>Why are boys like this?!</i>

00:59.210 --> 01:01.150
<i>It's love, dang it!</i>

01:04.770 --> 01:10.410
You know, when I'm with Takada-kun,
 I can feel my chest tighten up lately.

01:10.410 --> 01:11.030
<i>That's love!</i>

01:11.030 --> 01:12.340
<i>Love, love!</i>

01:11.960 --> 01:13.510
<b>Love</b>

01:12.340 --> 01:13.550
<i>Love explains it all!</i>

01:13.830 --> 01:15.630
<i>How frustrating!</i>

02:44.050 --> 02:48.020
My <b>Clueless</b> First Friend

02:49.060 --> 02:54.480
<i>Episode 13 "10 Years Later, the Same as Today"</i>

03:05.750 --> 03:08.720
<i>I have but one mission!</i>

03:11.380 --> 03:13.290
Ah, Takada-kun.

03:14.880 --> 03:17.420
<i>I must see it through, no matter what...</i>

03:21.860 --> 03:27.090
<i>and quickly find the bomb that's 
been planted in this classroom!</i>

03:29.770 --> 03:32.190
<b>— Going back in time a bit —</b>

03:34.020 --> 03:35.900
<b><i>PonPon</i></b>

03:34.020 --> 03:35.900
<b>Shampoo{right}</b>

03:34.020 --> 03:35.900
<b>Yonday</b>

03:34.520 --> 03:37.520
What <i>is</i> this place, Kitagawa-kun?!

03:38.510 --> 03:41.850
This is our base as the Scorpion Gang!

03:44.320 --> 03:47.260
Your base?! That's so awesome!

03:47.570 --> 03:50.610
This classroom fell into disuse 
because of declining birth rates,

03:50.610 --> 03:53.570
so we of the Scorpion Gang have claimed it!

03:54.090 --> 03:56.070
Without telling the teachers!

03:56.070 --> 04:00.460
You mean it's a secret room open only 
to those who have made a pledge?!

04:00.460 --> 04:02.120
That's the coolest!

04:02.120 --> 04:03.660
You could say that!

04:04.840 --> 04:06.760
Sure is cool.

04:06.760 --> 04:09.030
Made yourself at home 
right away, huh, Takada?

04:09.350 --> 04:12.350
So, why did you let me in here?

04:12.350 --> 04:16.610
I thought the Grim Reaper's friends 
weren't allowed in the Scorpion Gang.

04:20.320 --> 04:22.050
You see...

04:23.910 --> 04:24.920
Takada!

04:24.920 --> 04:26.760
Do us a once-in-a-lifetime favor!

04:26.760 --> 04:30.410
Please save our Scorpion Gang!

04:32.150 --> 04:34.840
We of the Scorpion Gang of class 5-1...

04:34.840 --> 04:38.660
have been caught up in an endless war 
against the Lizard Gang in class 2!

04:38.660 --> 04:40.540
Th-The Lizard Gang?!

04:40.910 --> 04:44.170
Fighting to grab the dodgeball 
court during recess...

04:44.560 --> 04:46.590
Umbrella duels on rainy days...

04:47.290 --> 04:50.440
Trying to climb the stairs skipping 
as many steps as possible...

04:50.440 --> 04:52.800
We've battled them countless times!

04:52.800 --> 04:55.480
But we always end up losing.

04:55.480 --> 04:58.280
They always pull something unfair.

04:58.280 --> 05:00.720
For such sacred contests?!

05:00.720 --> 05:01.750
That's terrible!

05:01.750 --> 05:05.760
Which is why, in order to put
the cowardly Lizard Gang in their place,

05:05.760 --> 05:07.730
we came up with <i>this</i>!

05:08.860 --> 05:11.880
I call it... the roach bomb!

05:12.460 --> 05:15.530
We customized an automatic pet feeder

05:15.530 --> 05:17.780
so the roaches inside
come flying out on a timer!

05:17.780 --> 05:19.410
It's the ultimate weapon!

05:19.380 --> 05:21.750
<b>ROACHES</b>

05:19.410 --> 05:21.370
I-Incredible!

05:21.920 --> 05:26.700
I'll have you know that's a custom mod
by yours truly, Tanaka the Engineer.

05:26.700 --> 05:31.260
Keeping those roaches trapped 
in there took a bit of finesse!

05:31.260 --> 05:33.780
A custom mod! Finesse!

05:33.780 --> 05:37.190
By planting it in the enemy leader's locker,

05:35.520 --> 05:38.020
<b>Ishida</b>

05:37.190 --> 05:40.460
we were sure it would make everyone hate him!

05:40.460 --> 05:43.280
We were so certain of our victory.

05:45.000 --> 05:46.350
However...

06:19.970 --> 06:22.220
The locker he planted it in...

06:22.220 --> 06:24.050
was the wrong one!

06:24.050 --> 06:25.030
What?!

06:25.430 --> 06:27.440
Yamamoto-kun?!

06:27.440 --> 06:31.400
Who'd have expected a miscalculation like 
that from me, Yamamoto the Informant?

06:31.400 --> 06:33.890
More like just a slip-up, right?!

06:33.890 --> 06:37.250
Wait, is the favor you want to ask me...

06:37.250 --> 06:38.070
That's right!

06:38.400 --> 06:41.500
Recover the bomb before time runs out!

06:41.780 --> 06:43.380
Why me, though?

06:44.250 --> 06:45.690
Well...

06:48.420 --> 06:51.090
<b>Nishimura</b>

06:51.080 --> 06:52.970
I know you can pull it off.

06:53.420 --> 06:59.050
Retrieve the bomb from Nishimura's 
locker without anyone noticing.

06:59.050 --> 07:01.470
Nishimura-san's in danger...

07:01.470 --> 07:03.660
D-Don't get me wrong here!

07:03.660 --> 07:06.770
We're not asking because we 
want to help the Grim Reaper.

07:07.100 --> 07:10.500
We just don't want 
to get civilians involved.

07:10.500 --> 07:11.360
Okay!

07:11.360 --> 07:15.160
So don't let Nishimura find 
out about the roaches!

07:15.160 --> 07:18.320
It would be cruel to scare 
Nishimura-san like that!

07:18.320 --> 07:19.290
Not what I meant!

07:19.290 --> 07:19.990
Got it!

07:19.990 --> 07:21.760
I'll do it!

07:23.630 --> 07:26.130
<b>— 10 minutes until expected detonation time —</b>

07:31.630 --> 07:35.630
<i>That's right. We don't 
want to help Nishimura.</i>

07:35.950 --> 07:37.890
<i>In fact, </i>we'll<i> be the ones who need help</i>

07:37.890 --> 07:41.350
<i>if the teachers find out and scold 
the living daylights out of us!</i>

07:41.760 --> 07:43.830
<i>Don't you mess this up, Takada!</i>

07:45.410 --> 07:46.770
Nishimura-san.

07:48.770 --> 07:51.860
Have you seen a bomb about this big?

07:53.820 --> 07:54.620
You—

07:54.620 --> 07:57.850
Ah! She's not supposed to find out!

07:57.850 --> 07:59.700
<i>You idiot! Don't look over here!</i>

07:59.700 --> 08:01.870
<i>Why'd you go and ruin it all?!</i>

08:01.870 --> 08:04.170
What's this about a bomb?

08:04.370 --> 08:06.610
<i>Talk your way out of it!</i>

08:06.610 --> 08:07.740
<i>Just don't say it!</i>

08:07.740 --> 08:11.340
<i>Don't slip up and mention 
the bomb with roaches inside!</i>

08:11.340 --> 08:14.280
Y-Y'know, a bomb.

08:14.280 --> 08:15.520
The kind that kills people.

08:15.520 --> 08:18.090
<i>Why are you making it sound worse?!</i>

08:18.090 --> 08:21.530
Um, I-I haven't seen any.

08:21.530 --> 08:23.320
I-Is that so?

08:23.320 --> 08:25.930
Good thing Takada acts 
so stupid to begin with.

08:25.930 --> 08:28.070
She didn't pry any further.

08:28.070 --> 08:29.200
Yeah.

08:29.200 --> 08:31.690
H-Hold on, Takada!

08:31.690 --> 08:33.440
Did you just say...

08:33.440 --> 08:37.000
that there's a bomb planted 
in the classroom?!

08:37.320 --> 08:39.500
<i>Hino!</i>

08:39.500 --> 08:40.890
Wait, huh? What's going on?

08:40.890 --> 08:44.480
They said there's a bomb 
planted in the classroom.

08:44.480 --> 08:45.750
For real?

08:45.750 --> 08:47.840
<i>Th-This is bad!</i>

08:47.840 --> 08:49.560
Shouldn't we run away?!

08:48.840 --> 08:55.930
<b>— 5 minutes until expected detonation time —</b>

08:49.560 --> 08:51.340
We should tell the teachers.

08:51.340 --> 08:55.940
In this situation, should we call 
the police or the fire department?

08:56.950 --> 08:59.270
<i>We're screwed now!</i>

09:00.390 --> 09:02.270
I-It's okay!

09:02.270 --> 09:04.520
I'll defuse the bomb.

09:04.520 --> 09:05.680
You will, Takada-kun?!

09:05.680 --> 09:06.830
Defuse a bomb?!

09:06.830 --> 09:07.930
Whew!

09:07.930 --> 09:10.150
You really are something, Takada!

09:10.150 --> 09:12.410
Teach me how to defuse bombs sometime!

09:12.410 --> 09:17.550
A grade schooler could never defuse 
a device as complex as a time bomb!

09:17.550 --> 09:18.900
A device...?

09:18.900 --> 09:22.150
That's right! We can't let 
Takada-kun sacrifice himself!

09:22.150 --> 09:24.390
We should all evacuate to the school yard!

09:24.390 --> 09:27.690
<i>Wait, Kasahara, you're really 
gonna act as class rep </i>now<i>?!</i>

09:27.930 --> 09:29.130
Dang it!

09:29.400 --> 09:31.520
We're running out of time!

09:31.520 --> 09:34.240
We've looked so hard, 
but we still haven't found it!

09:34.240 --> 09:36.670
<i>No, you haven't looked at all!</i>

09:36.670 --> 09:42.260
<i>Do whatever you have to and check 
Nishimura's locker already!</i>

09:42.260 --> 09:43.630
<i>Could it be?</i>

09:44.190 --> 09:45.440
Takada-kun.

09:45.790 --> 09:48.060
It'll be okay, Nishimura-san.

09:48.060 --> 09:49.570
I'll protect you!

09:49.570 --> 09:51.190
Never mind that.

09:51.190 --> 09:55.330
I-I found a weird device 
in my locker earlier.

09:53.590 --> 09:56.200
<b>Nishimura</b>

09:56.190 --> 09:59.320
If you're talking about that,
 I gave it to Sensei.

10:05.950 --> 10:09.460
<b>— 1 minute until expected detonation time —</b>

10:11.080 --> 10:13.570
Sensei's gonna die!

10:15.680 --> 10:17.090
Takada!

10:17.390 --> 10:19.540
We need to hurry up and find Sensei!

10:19.540 --> 10:21.170
He's going to die!

10:21.540 --> 10:23.990
Hang on, you know what's really going on here!

10:23.990 --> 10:25.940
Although Sensei <i>is</i> in for it!

10:25.940 --> 10:28.510
We just have to leave it to Takada now.

10:28.510 --> 10:31.330
There isn't much time left
before it's supposed to go off.

10:32.160 --> 10:33.660
Either way, after him!

10:34.930 --> 10:36.360
Darn it!

10:36.360 --> 10:39.440
Why is that moron the fastest in our grade?!

10:39.700 --> 10:42.490
<i>Will he be able to fool Sensei somehow?</i>

10:42.490 --> 10:44.690
<i>No... I've gotta believe in him!</i>

10:44.690 --> 10:46.720
<i>It's all up to you, Takada!</i>

10:47.070 --> 10:49.800
Didn't I tell you not to run in the halls?

10:49.800 --> 10:50.930
I'm sorry.

10:50.930 --> 10:53.510
<i>He was this close by?!</i>

10:55.360 --> 10:57.230
Sensei, that...

10:57.230 --> 10:59.000
Oh, this?

10:59.000 --> 11:01.390
Nishimura brought it to me earlier.

11:01.790 --> 11:05.450
But what's an automatic pet 
feeder doing at school?

11:05.870 --> 11:07.820
S-Sensei!

11:08.440 --> 11:10.990
Hey, no running in the halls!

11:10.990 --> 11:13.240
N-Now's really not the time for...

11:13.240 --> 11:15.740
What are you talking about, Kitagawa?

11:15.740 --> 11:17.400
Seriously, you guys...

11:17.400 --> 11:18.740
Form a line right there.

11:19.140 --> 11:20.190
Now listen up.

11:20.190 --> 11:21.190
Takada-kun...

11:20.190 --> 11:22.250
You'll soon be the oldest kids in school,

11:21.190 --> 11:22.250
Is everything all right?

11:22.650 --> 11:26.600
so you all need to get your acts together.

11:28.650 --> 11:29.690
Sensei...

11:47.120 --> 11:49.720
<i>The roach bomb, detonated.</i>

11:49.720 --> 11:52.610
<i>And the Scorpion Gang...</i>

11:49.730 --> 11:52.600
<b>Off limits</b>

11:53.240 --> 11:54.910
<i>wiped out.</i>

11:58.220 --> 12:00.070
What an awful experience.

12:00.070 --> 12:03.110
Seriously, those stupid boys...

12:04.080 --> 12:06.440
The mortal enemy of all ramen shops...

12:08.330 --> 12:11.230
Y-You sure did get a real earful.

12:11.230 --> 12:12.250
Yeah.

12:14.250 --> 12:17.740
But I'm glad you were safe, Nishimura-san!

12:18.180 --> 12:19.550
Thanks.

12:19.550 --> 12:23.720
For trying to get the bomb out of my locker.

12:23.720 --> 12:24.950
It was nothing!

12:24.950 --> 12:27.100
I got to see the Scorpion Gang's base,

12:27.100 --> 12:29.770
and I had fun playing with 
Kitagawa-kun and the others!

12:29.770 --> 12:32.880
No man can resist a secret base!

12:32.880 --> 12:34.950
Even though they made us clean it up!

12:35.270 --> 12:38.130
H-Huh, that sounds impressive.

12:38.130 --> 12:43.390
Oh, and they asked if I wanna join 
the new Neo Scorpion Gang they're forming!

12:43.920 --> 12:48.320
A-Are you going to join the Scorpion Gang?

12:49.160 --> 12:50.420
Nope, I won't.

12:50.810 --> 12:54.910
After all, the Scorpion Gang 
doesn't have you in it!

12:57.250 --> 13:01.760
I like the Grim Reaper 
a lot more than scorpions!

13:02.660 --> 13:04.890
I-Is that right?

13:04.890 --> 13:08.000
Yep! The Grim Reaper is the absolute coolest.

13:08.000 --> 13:09.730
Oh, I know!

13:09.730 --> 13:12.420
Wanna make a Grim Reaper Gang instead?

13:12.420 --> 13:14.690
We can invite Hino-kun and the others!

13:14.690 --> 13:16.320
Huh?!

13:17.980 --> 13:22.990
My <b>Clueless</b> First Friend

13:24.030 --> 13:29.990
Okay, today, use your imaginations 
and draw yourself ten years from now.

13:25.490 --> 13:29.990
The Future

13:40.760 --> 13:41.870
Tank top!

13:46.980 --> 13:49.250
I can't think of anything.

13:49.880 --> 13:51.840
Check it out, Nishimura-san!

13:52.140 --> 13:54.090
It's me ten years from now!

13:55.350 --> 13:56.840
I'm there, too?!

13:57.080 --> 14:01.280
This is me as an adult after I've acquired 
the magic spear Dark Dancer!

14:01.280 --> 14:03.860
Chosen as a high-ranking
member of the darkness!

14:03.860 --> 14:07.440
Wh-Why am I next to you?

14:08.270 --> 14:10.560
Because I want to be with you forever.

14:10.560 --> 14:12.150
With me?!

14:12.490 --> 14:15.550
I'd be really sad if you ever went away!

14:16.120 --> 14:18.460
I-I see...

14:19.930 --> 14:22.920
Takada-kun, what's this?

14:22.920 --> 14:26.260
That's your ectoplasm.

14:26.640 --> 14:29.300
<i>My... What?</i>

14:29.300 --> 14:31.810
It's your ectoplasm!

14:31.810 --> 14:34.140
My ectoplasm?

14:34.140 --> 14:37.570
This is ten years down the road,
so I think that's the least you can manage.

14:37.570 --> 14:40.260
I'm sure your Grim Reaper skills 
will have gone up, too.

14:40.260 --> 14:43.370
I-I don't look very cute.

14:43.650 --> 14:47.160
Well, you <i>are</i> usually way too cute.

14:47.160 --> 14:50.580
I had to draw you like this
so you'd look cool.

14:51.670 --> 14:52.790
I'm sorry!

14:52.790 --> 14:55.860
If only I could draw cooler pictures...

14:55.860 --> 14:58.160
N-No...

14:58.160 --> 15:02.670
<i>He said I'm usually way too cute!</i>

15:05.670 --> 15:08.670
My <b>Clueless</b> First Friend

15:16.420 --> 15:18.000
Takada-kun?

15:18.440 --> 15:21.500
S-Something smells really nice!

15:21.500 --> 15:22.330
Huh?

15:22.660 --> 15:25.060
You smell nicer than you always do!

15:25.060 --> 15:27.110
"A-Always"?!

15:27.110 --> 15:28.090
Um...

15:28.090 --> 15:32.330
Oh, i-is it because I switched shampoo?

15:32.330 --> 15:33.790
Shampoo?

15:33.790 --> 15:37.670
Yeah. My dad got some from someone at work.

15:37.670 --> 15:39.880
He said it's the fancy kind.

15:39.880 --> 15:42.040
Huh, is that so?

15:42.440 --> 15:45.350
No wonder you smell so good!

15:45.350 --> 15:47.310
D-Don't do that!

15:47.310 --> 15:48.800
It's embarrassing...

15:49.320 --> 15:51.050
Sorry, I couldn't help it.

15:51.050 --> 15:53.900
Why don't you keep on using this one?

15:53.900 --> 15:56.140
Although the usual is nice, too!

15:56.950 --> 16:01.810
I don't think I should use one 
that you can tell by its smell.

16:01.810 --> 16:03.650
Huh? Why not?

16:03.650 --> 16:07.910
If I do, I'm sure everyone 
will just laugh at me

16:08.290 --> 16:12.160
and say that the Grim Reaper 
shouldn't try to win over boys.

16:12.160 --> 16:13.990
That's a good point!

16:13.990 --> 16:14.670
Huh?!

16:14.670 --> 16:19.540
I mean, the Grim Reaper already has 
charm in a way other people don't!

16:21.940 --> 16:26.470
You're always so wonderful that 
I have to let everyone know!

16:32.630 --> 16:34.400
It's incredible.

16:34.400 --> 16:37.630
Having so much charm without 
doing anything extra...

16:37.630 --> 16:39.800
There's no one else out there like that!

16:39.800 --> 16:41.480
Th-That's not...

16:41.900 --> 16:45.730
This's just gotta be your charm curse!

16:45.730 --> 16:50.030
Even without the fancy shampoo, 
I wouldn't be able to stop thinking about you!

16:50.030 --> 16:52.050
S-So...

16:52.050 --> 16:54.740
So there are curses like that, too, huh?

16:54.740 --> 16:57.740
My <b>Clueless</b> First Friend

17:02.680 --> 17:04.640
I'm so bored.

17:06.420 --> 17:08.630
Nishimura-san

17:06.420 --> 17:08.630
Nishimura-san

17:06.420 --> 17:08.630
Good morning. What are you up to now?

17:08.920 --> 17:10.570
Whoa!

17:10.570 --> 17:13.540
A message from Nishimura-san!

17:13.540 --> 17:16.740
I-I ended up sending him a message...

17:17.530 --> 17:22.450
<i>I'm not being a bother for sending
a message for no good reason, am I?</i>

17:23.560 --> 17:28.310
Takada-kun

17:23.560 --> 17:28.310
Read

17:23.560 --> 17:28.310
Good morning. What are you up to now?

17:23.570 --> 17:27.910
<i>I-It says he read it, but he hasn't replied.</i>

17:28.750 --> 17:30.820
Why did I even send him that?

17:36.150 --> 17:37.850
Takada-kun...

17:37.850 --> 17:40.110
Maybe he took that rumor to heart.

17:41.360 --> 17:45.730
<i>You need to forward messages from 
the Grim Reaper to twenty people.</i>

17:45.730 --> 17:48.400
<i>Or else you'll end up with super bad luck!</i>

17:50.300 --> 17:52.300
Onee-chan! Onee-chan!

17:52.300 --> 17:55.600
I got a cursed message from Nishimura-san!

17:55.990 --> 17:58.130
A cursed message, you say?

17:58.130 --> 18:04.520
Messages from Nishimura-san
can be fatal in the most extreme cases!

18:04.520 --> 18:07.470
That's what the girls in our class said!

18:07.470 --> 18:10.280
Whoo, the most powerful curse!

18:10.280 --> 18:11.480
Yay!

18:12.840 --> 18:15.630
Nishimura-san <i>is</i> an angel, after all.

18:15.630 --> 18:19.950
You're so happy to hear from her
that you could just die, right?

18:20.690 --> 18:21.650
I get it!

18:24.620 --> 18:27.370
Takada-kun

18:24.620 --> 18:27.370
Thanks for the message, Nishimura-san!!
I'm so happy I could die!!{right}

18:27.370 --> 18:29.480
No, you're exaggerating!

18:30.260 --> 18:32.750
She replied, 
"You're exaggerating, Takada-kun."

18:32.750 --> 18:34.970
But it's the truth! What do I do?

18:34.970 --> 18:36.510
Hold that thought for a bit.

18:36.510 --> 18:40.170
I'm busy right now taking down this boss!

18:42.680 --> 18:44.680
<b>I'm not</b>

18:46.680 --> 18:49.140
I'm not exaggerating, Nishimura-san! After all, you're

18:49.140 --> 18:51.020
An angel!!

18:51.870 --> 18:53.900
Seriously, you're exaggerating!

18:53.900 --> 18:55.770
That's going way too far!

18:57.810 --> 19:02.130
<i>Everyone else thinks my messages are
tidings of misfortune from the Grim Reaper.</i>

19:02.790 --> 19:04.070
That's right!

19:04.070 --> 19:09.420
I need to let twenty people know that
I got a message from Nishimura-san!

19:09.420 --> 19:11.980
Huh? What's with that rule?

19:11.980 --> 19:13.690
They want you to brag?

19:13.690 --> 19:14.860
What do I do?

19:14.860 --> 19:17.830
I don't have that many people's contact info!

19:17.830 --> 19:20.940
In that case, just tell folks at school.

19:20.940 --> 19:23.880
And not just twenty of them. Tell everyone!

19:23.880 --> 19:25.310
I see!

19:25.310 --> 19:28.750
Yay! Maybe I'll become super-popular!

19:28.750 --> 19:30.550
You're so smart, Onee-chan!

19:31.400 --> 19:33.610
Right? Right?!

19:33.610 --> 19:35.820
He's as energetic as ever.

19:39.330 --> 19:43.330
Listen to this! I got a 
message from Nishimura-san!

19:43.330 --> 19:44.320
Huh?

19:44.940 --> 19:48.030
I'm so happy, it feels 
like I'm walking on air!

19:48.030 --> 19:49.170
And then...

19:49.170 --> 19:51.910
I'm as happy as can be! Yay!

19:54.540 --> 19:55.910
Nishimura-san.

19:56.970 --> 19:59.630
Would you mind giving me your contact info?

20:00.870 --> 20:04.500
S-Sure, but why all of a sudden?

20:04.760 --> 20:09.440
Getting a message from you 
will lead to happiness.

20:09.440 --> 20:11.240
That's what everyone's saying.

20:12.160 --> 20:14.610
I'm over the moon!

20:15.350 --> 20:17.240
Hey, you, listen to this!

21:52.350 --> 21:54.490
Nishimura-san!

21:54.830 --> 21:56.620
Good morning!

21:56.620 --> 21:59.390
G-Good morning, Takada-kun.

21:59.390 --> 22:01.700
Your dad's with you today!

22:01.700 --> 22:03.710
O-Only for a little bit.

22:04.350 --> 22:05.790
Good morning to you!

22:05.790 --> 22:07.850
Good morning, Taiyou-kun.

22:08.370 --> 22:09.840
Oh, oh, Nishimura-san!

22:10.130 --> 22:11.970
How was your daily horoscope today?

22:11.970 --> 22:14.360
Well, it was the worst of the lot...

22:17.480 --> 22:19.830
Ah, you meant Akane, didn't you?

22:20.980 --> 22:24.190
Oh, yeah, both of you are Nishimura-san!

22:25.100 --> 22:27.250
It's confusing with the two of us.

22:27.450 --> 22:30.490
Then, I'll call you Akane-chan, just for now!

22:30.490 --> 22:31.190
Huh?

22:31.750 --> 22:33.870
Good morning, Akane-chan!

22:33.870 --> 22:36.240
How was your daily horoscope today?

22:37.640 --> 22:39.710
Um, well...

22:39.710 --> 22:43.770
I-It said there may be 
good things in my future,

22:44.210 --> 22:46.210
T-Taiyou-kun.

22:49.050 --> 22:49.860
<i>Huh?</i>

22:50.550 --> 22:54.200
<i>Is there any reason Akane 
needs to call him Taiyou-kun?</i>

22:54.560 --> 22:58.140
U-Using first names is a 
little embarrassing, huh?

22:58.620 --> 23:00.320
You think so?

23:00.320 --> 23:02.920
I love Akane-chan!

23:02.920 --> 23:04.820
You mean my name, right?

23:12.840 --> 23:14.360
Okay, let's get going.

23:14.360 --> 23:15.580
You two will end up late.

23:15.580 --> 23:16.350
Yeah.

23:16.350 --> 23:17.250
Let's go!

23:34.970 --> 23:39.970
<b>Thank you for watching!!</b>
